{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the people did not journey.</b> It suspended the matter upon the people and did not say ״וְלֹא נָסַע הָעָם,״ to inform that the people agreed not to journey until Miriam was gathered in. And even though the matter depended on the journeying of the cloud, the Torah testifies that also in her merit they were desirous of the delay to honor her — and all the more so since it was known to them that in her merit they had the water (Ta'anit 9a); surely the people would sit there by the water." "<b>Thus concludes the pericah of BeHa'alotekha.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:12.713780842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}